Henry J Cobb wrote:
> Far too many items become almost useless once you have one unicorn horn.

Let's not be vague here.  Which items exactly are you thinking of?

> Spellbooks of Cure Blindness (and carrots) will finally be useful.

Currently, the spells of Cure Blindness, Cure Sickness, and carrots are
all 100% effective at repairing the problem in question on the first
try... if you successfully cast the spell, of course.

A blessed unicorn horn does not always 'hit' on the first try; an
uncursed one 'hits' less often than that.  In addition, if you have
multiple problems (stunned, confused, and ill, for example), it is not
guaranteed to repair the particular one that you want fixed.

This has been fatal to players on NAO in the past who were over-reliant
on the horn.

While it's certainly possible that unicorn horns are too "all-purpose",
you really need to make a better case than this.  Right now, most of
your YANI posts are ill-thought-out and poorly supported; you generally
fail to demonstrate that there's a need for a change before haring off
headlong into the details of the change.  Take, for example, the current
post I'm responding to, and the simple counterargument:

Why should improving the utility of Cure Blindness take priority over
improving the utility of Detect Foot, Invisibility, Levitation, or
similar -- the first of which is simply directly useless, and the other
two are also rendered less useful by easily-obtainable items in the game?

